The accompanying LICENSE.uefi-md5sum contains the license text.

Project and corresponding source: https://github.com/pbatard/uefi-md5sum
The Linux port embeds the unchanged standalone EFI applications already
distributed with this Rufus source tree in res/md5: ia32, x64, arm, aa64,
riscv64 and loongarch64. They are installed on the selected media only when
runtime UEFI validation is requested. The Linux application does not execute
these EFI applications on its host.

The original Rufus application license remains in LICENSE.txt.
